"""Scenario templates for E1 (docs/plans/PLAN.md §9).

Each template describes one decision between a *risky* option (wider outcome
range: higher best case, lower worst case) and a *safe* option (narrower
range). Numbers are never written here: the generator draws probabilities and
payoffs on a grid, computes expected values exactly and renders the text.

Per option:
  label        short name shown in the option list
  act          verb phrase after "chose to"
  good / bad   present-tense branch descriptions ("the surgery succeeds")
  past_good / past_bad   the same branch reported as an outcome
  facts        (fact, source, time) triples for control items: a fact that makes
               this option's bad branch much more likely and that the
               decision-maker could cheaply have checked before deciding
  causes       for luck twins: a cause of the bad branch that nothing available
               at decision time could have revealed

Unit kinds: ``gain`` values are shown as ``mult * base``; ``cost`` values are
shown as ``mult * (100 - base)`` so minimising expected cost is the same as
maximising expected base value.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

UNITS = {
    # name: (kind, low-stakes multiplier, high-stakes multiplier, objective phrase)
    "qaly": ("gain", 0.1, 0.4, "maximise the patient's expected quality-adjusted life years (QALYs)"),
    "money_gain": ("gain", 1, 20, "maximise expected net profit"),
    "money_cost": ("cost", 1, 20, "minimise the expected total cost"),
    "downtime_hours": ("cost", 0.1, 1, "minimise the expected hours of service downtime"),
    "points": ("gain", 1, 10, "maximise the expected task score (in points)"),
}

